  "question": "For p-tolualdehyde and TBHP with TBAI in MeCN, what initial conditions and validation priorities are supported by the reference apparent parameters and literature evidence?",
  "scientific_facts": [
    {
      "id": "F1",
      "text": "The target reaction is p-tolualdehyde with TBHP to form the corresponding perester. The aldehyde-to-perester reaction class is supported by the literature record (DOI: 10.1039/C1CC14602E). Its aqueous literature conditions do not establish the kinetics of the proposed flow system.",
      "role": "analogy",
      "required": true,
      "evidence_ids": [
        "route:tbpb_benzaldehyde",
        "kinetics:tbpb_benzaldehyde",
        "ScreenedCondition:tbpb_benzaldehyde",
        "literature:aldehyde_peresters_2011"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "text": "Main reaction: apparent Ea = 4.495 kJ/mol, ln A = -4.1700, orders catalyst 3.942, benzaldehyde 3.947, TBHP 2.530. These parameters describe the calibrated system and do not establish an elementary mechanism.",
      "role": "parameters",
      "required": true,
      "evidence_ids": [
        "route:tbpb_benzaldehyde",
        "kinetics:tbpb_benzaldehyde",
        "ScreenedCondition:tbpb_benzaldehyde",
        "literature:aldehyde_peresters_2011"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "text": "In the Route 4 reference, the fixed-composition rate multiplier across its measured temperature range is 1.106. A 10% catalyst increase multiplies the rate by 1.456; uniform 10% dilution of reactants and catalyst gives 0.334. These reference sensitivities motivate concentration and mixing checks; they are not fitted values for the new substrate.",
      "role": "explanation",
      "required": true,
      "evidence_ids": [
        "route:tbpb_benzaldehyde",
        "kinetics:tbpb_benzaldehyde",
        "ScreenedCondition:tbpb_benzaldehyde",
        "literature:aldehyde_peresters_2011"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "text": "A proposed calibration grid uses temperatures 45/55/65 °C and residence times 371.10/742.20/1484.41 s (9 combinations). The reference TBHP/aldehyde ratio is 1.1 and catalyst concentration 0.3160 mol/L. Feasible concentrations and solvent compatibility must be checked for the new substrate.",
      "role": "decision",
      "required": true,
      "evidence_ids": [
        "route:tbpb_benzaldehyde",
        "kinetics:tbpb_benzaldehyde",
        "ScreenedCondition:tbpb_benzaldehyde",
        "literature:aldehyde_peresters_2011"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "text": "The para-methyl substituent may alter reactivity, but no substituent effect is calibrated. Measure target perester, residual aldehyde/TBHP and possible by-products before fitting the new system. Reference bootstrap intervals are not new-substrate confidence intervals.",
